# Keeps the Docker build context small and secrets out of the image.
# Exists because the repo root holds two Windows virtualenvs and a .git history that would
# otherwise be shipped into every build, and .env which must never enter an image layer.
# Only requirements files are actually COPYed; project code arrives by bind mount at run time.

.venv/
.venv-dbt/
.git/
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
**/__pycache__/
**/target/
**/logs/
data/raw/*.csv
dashboards/
